From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kernel <noreply@localhost>
Date: Thu, 6 Nov 2026 22:10:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: topaz: instantiate the ADSP loader

The driver landed in 0027 but nothing instantiates it, so
/sys/kernel/boot_adsp/ never appears and the ROM's userspace
cannot start the ADSP the way it does on the stock kernel.

The stock FDT has the node and it is small:

  qcom,msm-adsp-loader {
          compatible = "qcom,adsp-loader";
          qcom,rproc-handle = <0x1bb>;   /* ADSP PAS */
          qcom,adsp-state = <0x0>;
          status = "ok";
  };

Add the same contract under &remoteproc_adsp, which is the node
the software phandle resolves to and the one the loader needs
to see registered before it binds (it returns -EPROBE_DEFER
until then). Place it as a child of the PAS node so the phandle
is local and the load order falls out of the device tree.

auto_boot stays off on the PAS node: booting is now the
loader's job, exactly like downstream. Nothing here boots the
ADSP by itself - the write to boot_adsp/boot does, and that
write comes from Android userspace, not from this kernel.

Compile-only: firmware presence and the boot/ssr sysfs
contract are hardware-verification items.

Signed-off-by: Kernel <noreply@localhost>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6225-xiaomi-topaz.dts | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6225-xiaomi-topaz.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6225-xiaomi-topaz.dts
index aad834584..046bcf82b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6225-xiaomi-topaz.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6225-xiaomi-topaz.dts
@@ -510,6 +510,21 @@ irled@1 {
 &remoteproc_adsp {
 	firmware-name = "adsp.mdt";
 	status = "okay";
+
+	/*
+	 * Android userspace on this ROM boots the ADSP through
+	 * /sys/kernel/boot_adsp/boot, not through the generic
+	 * remoteproc state file (the vendor PAS resource ships
+	 * with auto_boot off). The driver is in this series
+	 * (qcom,adsp-loader); this node is what makes it exist.
+	 * qcom,adsp-state is the vendor hint for the initial
+	 * state and matches the live FDT.
+	 */
+	adsp_loader: adsp-loader {
+		compatible = "qcom,adsp-loader";
+		qcom,rproc-handle = <&remoteproc_adsp>;
+		qcom,adsp-state = <0>;
+	};
 };
 
